10. Lean follow-on (local 16 GB budget)

After repeated OOM crashes from full-chr Pan-UKB downloads (~2 GB compressed chr1 WBC), remaining work was re-run under LOCAL_COMPUTE.md constraints: region-only fetches, cached 500k samples, train caps, one job at a time.

10.1 Duffy / WBC (region-only)
Downloaded 0.3 MB Pan-UKB WBC window chr1:159.0-159.4 Mb (3,757 variants). Duffy neighborhood mean |beta_AFR-beta_EUR| exceeded flank/outside (passes_positive_control=True; duffy_wbc_region_positive_control.csv). This is a label-level positive control, not a full WBC genome-wide model.

10.2 Fine-map tiers (z_meta lead, unconfounded)
Lead = max |z_meta| within LD block. fine_mapped high-I2 rate ~0.32 (vs ~1.0 under old I2-lead heuristic). On cached sample: fine_mapped AUROC 0.639; tag_only 0.714; all 0.715 (ablation_finemap_tiers_zlead.csv). AF_LD_SEL predicts heterogeneity more in tag_only than in z-lead fine-mapped variants.

10.3 External validation (lean)
PAGE full FTP deferred. Local Pan-UKB LDL chr22 EUR vs AFR (n=80k): raw beta corr ~0; after dropping top 10% |beta_EUR-beta_AFR|, corr rises to 0.119 (95% CI 0.111-0.129; delta +0.124). Interpreting as: removing the most discordant effects improves cross-ancestry concordance — consistent with a triage story, with honest scope that this is not yet PAGE/GBMI FTP.

Hard rule going forward: use scripts/download_panukbb_region.py; never full-chr bgz on this rig.
